.TH WPM 8 "2026-11-25" "Wunix" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
wpm \- unified package manager for Wunix OS (.wp)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwpm\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]... [\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBwpm\fR is the unified package manager for Wunix OS. It manages base system components, the kernel, metapackages (\fBbase\fR, \fBbase-apps\fR, \fBminimal-live\fR), and user applications in \fB.wp\fR format.
.PP
The \fB[system]\fR repository source is built into \fBwpm\fR and cannot be modified by users. User application sources are configured in \fI/etc/wpm/sources.conf\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBinstall\fR \fIPKG\fR...
Install one or more packages or metapackages (supports dependencies).
.TP
\fBreinstall\fR \fIPKG\fR...
Force reinstall one or more already installed packages.
.TP
\fBremove\fR \fIPKG\fR...
Remove installed user packages (system/critical packages are protected).
.TP
\fBupdate\fR
Synchronize system and user repository indexes.
.TP
\fBupgrade\fR
Upgrade installed packages (including kernel A/B rotation).
.TP
\fBcheck\fR
Check for available updates.
.TP
\fBsearch\fR \fIQUERY\fR
Search packages across all repositories.
.TP
\fBlist\fR
List installed packages.
.TP
\fBinfo\fR \fIPKG\fR
Show package details.
.TP
\fBrepo\fR [\fBlist\fR|\fBadd\fR|\fBrm\fR|\fBping\fR]
Manage user repository sources (\fI/etc/wpm/sources.conf\fR).
.TP
\fBaudit\fR [\fB\-v\fR]
Audit kernel and system file integrity.
.TP
\fBkernel\fR [\fBlist\fR|\fBrollback\fR|\fBclean\fR]
Manage kernel binaries in \fI/boot\fR.
.TP
\fBclean\fR
Clean local cache \fI/var/cache/wpm\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show version information.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Confirm operations without prompting.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-critical\fR
Target critical system packages only.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose output.
.TP
\fB\-\-reinstall\fR
Reinstall already installed packages.
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-critical\-unsafe\fR
Bypass critical system update guard for user packages.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBwspd\fR(8), \fBwinstall\fR(8)
